+# ADR-0015: Cached copies of published data
+
+## Status
+Accepted (2026-11-12)
+
+Refines [ADR-0004](0004-local-persistence-strategy.md) for one kind of document; ADR-0004 is unchanged and keeps governing every document of user data. Driven by `add-remote-zone-rules-updates`.
+
+## Context
+
+ADR-0004 keeps the user's own data (locations, preferences) and says: "Invalid data never crashes the app: the UI shows the error state with a reset action" and "Writes are broadcast (`BroadcastChannel`, with the `storage` event as fallback); other tabs reload the changed document". That is right for data the user made and cannot get back.
+
+`add-remote-zone-rules-updates` stores a downloaded zone rules release on the device. It is not user data: the site publishes it, the app bundles an older or equal copy of it, and nothing is lost when it is dropped. An error state with a reset action would ask the user to repair what the app can repair alone, and a broadcast would add a second channel for a rare event.
+
+## Decision
+
+A document that is a cached copy of data the site publishes (the first is the stored zone rules release) keeps the ADR-0004 envelope `{ schemaVersion, payload }`, its repository port and its contract tests, and differs in three rules:
+
+1. When it cannot be read (invalid JSON, another schema version, a payload its reader rejects, storage that throws), it is removed silently and the bundled data is used. That is its recoverable state: it has no error state and no reset action.
+2. Its writes are not broadcast. Other tabs read it at their next check.
+3. A failed write is silent. The bundled data stays in use and the copy arrives with the next deploy.
+
+User data stays fully under ADR-0004.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Positive:
+- A damaged cache never blocks the app or asks the user for anything.
+- One rule for every future cached copy of published data.
+
+Negative:
+- Two persistence regimes to know; the cached-copy regime applies only to data the site can republish.
+
+## Alternatives Considered
+
+**Treat the stored release as user data (error state, reset, broadcast)**: asks the user to repair a copy the app can replace itself, and broadcasts a rare event. Rejected.
+
+**Edit ADR-0004**: `.claude/rules/adr.md` forbids editing an accepted ADR to change its decision. Rejected.
